/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Manifold absolute pressure (MAP) is the absolute pressure inside the intake manifold after the throttle, measured in kPa.
   - A MAP sensor turns pressure into voltage.
   - Vo ≈ (Vex ÷ 4) × (ΔR ÷ R)
   - Vo is bridge output in V; Vex is excitation voltage in V; R is gauge resistance in Ω; ΔR is its change in Ω.
   - A capacitive MAP sensor uses the diaphragm as one plate of a capacitor.
   - An air flow meter measures the air entering the engine.
   - Hot-wire and hot-film meters keep a heated element at a fixed temperature above the incoming air.
   - A Karman vortex meter places a bluff body in the air stream.
   - The speed-density method uses MAP, engine speed, displacement, volumetric efficiency and intake temperature.
   - ṁair = ηv × Pman × Vd × (N ÷ 2) ÷ (R × T)
*/
