/* book exam traps: For a 60-2 wheel the missing-tooth gap is 3T, not 2T. Two teeth are missing, but the interval from the last present tooth to the next present tooth covers three pitch periods. | Use the pitch count z (60 for 60-2, 36 for 36-1) in speed = 1/(zT). Do not use the number of present teeth (58 or 35) when you measure T between normal teeth. | VR amplitude changes with speed; a clean signal at 3000 rpm does not prove the sensor will work at 150 rpm cranking. Hall output amplitude does not depend on speed. | Angular position is an angle in degrees; angular speed is a rate in rpm. A timing sensor gives phase information, not necessarily a second independent speed signal. | Do not assume the first tooth after the gap is at TDC. Its offset is calibration data and varies between engines. */
